\ul{
\li{\strong{The seven rows of finding F3} that RV-3A names as the test of the second candidate: the six official accepts are accepted, \code{rv3a-gcd2-krule-eager-declaration-then-plain-bad} gets the official rejection (the first candidate accepted it from the memo), and the wrong rejection of the published mechanism, \code{rv3a-gcd2-pair-eager-then-plain-same-binder-ok}, is an accept: in place the comparison under the flag comes first, as it officially does.}
\li{\strong{Schedule} (F6 of RV-3B): the two exports of 300 theorems in the reviewer's finding directory, 50 runs each (1, 2, 4 and 8 workers, batch and pipelined loading, five times each through the executable; the JVM launcher with 8 workers, both loadings, five times), and all 48 exports of the reviewer's schedule family, 30 runs each: one verdict per export in every run, an accept. Under the union the pair is shown by the plain procedure in whatever session asks.}
\li{\strong{Real mutants} (RV-3B: 37 slices of declarations that hold an eager argument and 1,449 mutants with an official verdict; the 46 mutants of the heavy slice were left out, limits of 3 GiB heap and 120 s): the official verdict on all 1,486. In 54 of them the first candidate's machine had declined a unit: those are units that were still in progress on another worker when the first rejection ended the file (the machine's class \code{\verb~|E_CANCEL~}), and in one mutant two units that depend on the rejected declaration and end in an internal check of the machine (\code{\verb~|E_ILLTYPED~}; the published build declines the same two under the differential engine). They change from run to run - 36 of the 54 inputs showed one in two runs, for the first candidate and for the second - and none is a decline of eager reduction. The published build declines 238 units of the same inputs through its eager mechanism.}
\li{\strong{The eager family of the suite}, the 101 rows of section 5, machine alone in process, default set: \strong{64 official verdicts, 37 accepts of kind T rows, no wrong rejection, none declined}, beside 93 / 8 / 0 / 0 for the first candidate and 63 / 37 / 0 / 1 declined for the published mechanism. That is what the union costs in agreement: the 29 rows on which the first candidate gave the official rejection and the union accepts are rows whose pair is asked under the flag before any plain comparison of it (or in another declaration) and is true in plain mode. No row is rejected under any of five switch sets that the official checker accepts, and no row is accepted that is not of kind T.}
\li{\strong{A kind T class that section 10 did not name} (T1 of RV-3B): the machine writes an entry for an intermediate pair of lazy unfolding, which the official kernel does not cache. Under the union the class is part of the general one: a pair that is true in plain mode is true under the flag.}
}
}

